{
  "mn98:0.1": "Middle Discourses 98 ",
  "mn98:0.2": "With Vāseṭṭha ",
  "mn98:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn98:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying in a forest near Icchānaṅgala. ",
  "mn98:2.1": "Now at that time several very well-known well-to-do brahmins were residing in Icchānaṅgala. They included ",
  "mn98:2.2": "the brahmins Caṅkī, Tārukkha, Pokkharasāti, Jānussoṇi, Todeyya, and others. ",
  "mn98:3.1": "Then as the students Vāseṭṭha and Bhāradvāja were going for a walk they began to discuss the question: ",
  "mn98:3.2": "“How do you become a brahmin?” ",
  "mn98:3.3": "Bhāradvāja said this: ",
  "mn98:3.4": "“When you’re well born on both your mother’s and father’s side, stemming from a clean vessel, with irrefutable and impeccable genealogy back to the seventh paternal generation—",
  "mn98:3.5": "then you’re a brahmin.” ",
  "mn98:3.6": "Vāseṭṭha said this: ",
  "mn98:3.7": "“When you’re ethical and accomplished in doing your duties—",
  "mn98:3.8": "then you’re a brahmin.” ",
  "mn98:4.1": "But neither was able to persuade the other. ",
  "mn98:5.1": "So Vāseṭṭha said to Bhāradvāja, ",
  "mn98:5.2": "“Worthy Bhāradvāja, the ascetic Gotama—a Sakyan, gone forth from a Sakyan family—is staying in a forest near Icchānaṅgala. ",
  "mn98:5.3": "He has this good reputation: ",
  "mn98:5.4": "‘That Blessed One is perfected, a fully awakened Buddha, accomplished in knowledge and conduct, holy, knower of the world, supr